From db8b8abbe8bafb018ce135492298ec07f90f8c08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xuan.huang" <5563315+Huxpro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:37:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(motion): orchestrate variant children, controls and
 gestures

Mirror Motion's variant tree in the background: variant children register
with their closest variant node in mount order (components without
variants stay transparent), giving stagger index/total for
delayChildren: stagger(), staggerChildren and staggerDirection. Every
node opens a completion session per resolved definition, settled from the
main thread, so afterChildren waits for its subtree and automatic-duration
beforeChildren waits for the parent's real completion.

Add useAnimationControls/useAnimation for animate={controls}; start()
resolves once the bound components and their variant children finish, and
set() jumps without animating. whileTap/whileHover variant labels now
propagate to variant children through the same tree. stagger() is callable
from render code and still serializes as its Main Thread Function.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
